    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Creamy Cajun Chicken [with Cauliflower Rice]",
      "description": "This creamy Cajun chicken dish is rich and full of flavor. Served over low-carb cauliflower rice it’s simple to make and is great for busy weeknight dinners when you need to whip up something quick.\n\nAll you need to make this scrumptious dish is some chicken thighs, cauliflower to turn into rice, tin tomatoes, an onion, and a bunch of common herbs and spices. If you’re missing any of these herbs and spices, you can always add something else or leave it out entirely. The same goes for chicken thighs—breasts can be used instead.\n\nMaking this dish involves a few simple steps. You start by making the cauliflower rice in a blender (unless you have ready-made cauliflower rice). Once the rice is sorted, cook up the chicken in a skillet before adding the cream to make a thick and smooth sauce. If you don’t have any dairy cream or if you’re dairy-free, you can always use coconut cream instead. Once the chicken mixture is cooked, serve it with the rice in a bowl. Don’t forget to sprinkle some fresh herbs on top!\n\nThis dish will give you lots of important nutrients and is sure to satisfy even the most demanding appetite. It’s also a great dish to reheat the next day for lunch. If you’re looking for a tasty and healthy chicken recipe with a little bit of spice, give this one a go.\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\n20 ounce cauliflower, riced\n1/2 medium red onion\n1/4 cup olive oil, divided\n20 ounce boneless, skinless chicken thighs\n2 teaspoon paprika\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon dried oregano\n1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\nSalt and pepper to taste\n200 gram canned diced tomatoes\n1 cup heavy whipping cream\n1 teaspoon sea salt\n2 tablespoon fresh parsley, chopped\n\nNutrition Summary: This makes a total of 4 servings of Keto Creamy Cajun Chicken. Each serving comes out to be 578 calories, 48.7g fat, 6.9g net carbs, and 29.2g protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
